I took a look at your patch two weeks ago and I think it would be a 
usable solution. But it seemed to me that the number of turns could be 
lost if the killer-string is already very long. (probably not a big problem)

I think a cleaner solution would be to add an additional entry to the 
logfile-entry structure. (the same is true for e.g. my conduct-patch, 
but as long as I log only ascensions I don't run into a problem there).

Below I'll add a diff for topten.c that I wrote to get that done.

